00:23:19.231 --> 00:23:22.300 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's like the falling
empire of Rome.

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:24.536 align:start position:0%
You're watching the house
collapse or everything collapse

00:23:24.536 --> 00:23:25.670
around me, right?

00:23:27.773 --> 00:23:30.942
For me, the amount
of pride that I took

00:23:30.942 --> 00:23:33.211
in rebuilding my life ethically,

00:23:33.211 --> 00:23:35.414 align:start size:84% position:16%
I can't tell you what
that meant to me,

00:23:35.414 --> 00:23:37.816
to go out and prove to myself,

00:23:37.816 --> 00:23:41.520
to my children, not the
world, to my children,

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:43.655
that I would go out right again

00:23:43.655 --> 00:23:45.857
and just do things so
straight as an arrow

00:23:45.857 --> 00:23:47.826
and empower people
all over the world

00:23:47.826 --> 00:23:49.060
and make even more money.

00:23:50.228 --> 00:23:52.631
And that was something
that just kept me going

00:23:52.631 --> 00:23:54.132
in the early days.

00:23:54.132 --> 00:23:56.701
It just snowballed and fed
in itself and fed in itself.

00:23:58.170 --> 00:24:00.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, my life today is far
better than it ever was

00:24:00.639 --> 00:24:02.374
back in the craziest
times of Stratton.

00:24:02.374 --> 00:24:04.609
- Yeah, that's gotta
be a crazy retraining,

00:24:04.609 --> 00:24:07.345 align:start size:88% position:13%
to try to do things
fully on the up and up.

00:24:07.345 --> 00:24:08.847
We were gonna try
to do something,

00:24:08.847 --> 00:24:10.882
and I have a feeling we'll
do something in the future.

00:24:10.882 --> 00:24:12.684
But even when we were in
the little negotiations

00:24:12.684 --> 00:24:13.752 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then things
just moved too fast,

00:24:13.752 --> 00:24:14.986
you were basically like,

00:24:14.986 --> 00:24:16.621
"Just gimme something,
and I'll make it work."

00:24:16.621 --> 00:24:18.123
You didn't wanna negotiate.

00:24:18.123 --> 00:24:19.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were just like, "Let's
make it nice and easy."

00:24:19.357 --> 00:24:20.358
And then things just happened

00:24:20.358 --> 00:24:22.227
to move along in
a different way.

00:24:22.227 --> 00:24:24.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
But was that a
real shift for you?

00:24:24.796 --> 00:24:26.298
How you're gonna do business?

00:24:26.298 --> 00:24:28.400
Actually, how you're
gonna engage in that?

00:24:30.335 --> 00:24:31.603
- Yes and no.

00:24:31.603 --> 00:24:33.071
I think one of the
lessons I learned

00:24:33.071 --> 00:24:36.775
was that if you're a
really good negotiator

00:24:38.176 --> 00:24:40.479
and you negotiate a deal
where it's so great for you

00:24:40.479 --> 00:24:41.947
and bad for other people,

00:24:41.947 --> 00:24:43.849
that's not a good negotiation.

00:24:43.849 --> 00:24:45.217
It just ends up in a lawsuit,

00:24:45.217 --> 00:24:46.685
aka Steve Madden's shoes.

00:24:46.685 --> 00:24:48.487 align:start size:84% position:16%
When Steve came to
me, he was very young.

00:24:48.487 --> 00:24:51.289 align:start size:97% position:3%
He was naive, and I took his
company from him legally,

00:24:51.289 --> 00:24:54.326
and I took 85% because
he didn't know better.

00:24:54.326 --> 00:24:57.329 align:start size:97% position:3%
And all that did was created
animosity down the road.

00:24:57.329 --> 00:24:59.531
So I don't think a
great negotiation is

00:24:59.531 --> 00:25:01.700
when you get such a good deal

00:25:01.700 --> 00:25:03.702 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you fuck
everyone else over.

00:25:03.702 --> 00:25:08.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
And also, I just
refuse to cut corners.

00:25:08.273 --> 00:25:10.609 align:start size:84% position:16%
In my life, my value
system right now,

00:25:11.943 --> 00:25:15.046 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's based on creating
value for people.

00:25:15.046 --> 00:25:16.515
There's a reason
why I haven't...

00:25:16.515 --> 00:25:18.083
Everybody's "why haven't
you launched any NFTs yet?"

00:25:18.083 --> 00:25:19.684
There's a reason why I
haven't launched NFTs,

00:25:19.684 --> 00:25:21.887
'cause I'm not sure if
the market is ready.

00:25:21.887 --> 00:25:24.089
I know I'll make a
quick 10 million.

00:25:24.089 --> 00:25:25.357
But probably the
people who buy them

00:25:25.357 --> 00:25:26.992
might lose a quick 7 million.

00:25:26.992 --> 00:25:28.226
So I didn't do it.

00:25:29.361 --> 00:25:30.695 align:start size:84% position:16%
Yeah, I'd love to
have the extra money,

00:25:30.695 --> 00:25:31.530
but I have enough money.

00:25:31.530 --> 00:25:34.032
I'm not gonna engage

00:25:34.032 --> 00:25:36.601 align:start size:84% position:16%
